# Security & RBAC Enforcement Rules

## 1. PocketBase API Rules & ACL
- NEVER rely solely on UI component hiding for access control.
- `clinical_notes` collection MUST always be strictly restricted in PocketBase API Rules to Admin and the owning Doctor (`@request.auth.id = doctor.user`).
- Never expose confidential endpoints or patient profiles to `secretary`, `writer`, or `patient` roles.

## 2. SvelteKit Server Guards
- Always enforce role checks in `+layout.server.ts` or `+page.server.ts` before rendering protected routes (`/dashboard/*`).
- Redirect unauthorized users immediately to `/auth` or `/dashboard` base on their role level.

## 3. Data Privacy & Environment Safety
- NEVER expose `POCKETBASE_ADMIN_PASSWORD` or sensitive API keys to the client-side bundle.
- Audio recordings and medical files must be saved directly to PocketBase Storage with strict view permissions; NEVER persist raw audio or secret notes in browser `localStorage`.